{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-3299-7206-be01-3f31d31abf9c","id":"01a1a5f4-3054-76a9-bb60-57ad04f995a0","idempotency_key":"a73e55349b91c15eef791497f53103e74b0c43f00f125f6f184136e3227f95a1","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T09:46:46Z","payload":{"note":"Four of five done. docs/running.md (build, packaging/install.sh, environment variables and what each one degrades to, the tab list), docs/migrations.md (the v1..v6 chain, the v4 reset into legacy_sessions and the one-time notice, and the three places a session lives), docs/signing.md (the operator checklist: what an agent can finish with deliver/evidence record/evidence verify/sign resolve --dry-run, what only a person can with war sign - which refuses without a TTY per its own help - and the war admin doctor findings to decide about first), plus a Running the app section in README.md. packaging/install.sh builds the release binary, installs it and the frontend where static_dir() actually looks (<prefix>/share/rustybrickchess/frontend, not lib/), and writes a desktop entry. It also warns when the binary predates the newest source: here the release build was four days old and installed an app that reported schema 3 instead of 6, which is exactly the failure the warning exists to catch. Verified by installing into a temp prefix and running the installed binary against a brand-new database: {\"schema\":6}, GET / 200, wasm 200, /api/session/notice {\"reset\":false}. STILL OPEN: i-71ca (MCP setup and context/study format docs) - the MCP server does not exist yet (t-745d), so documenting its setup would describe something unbuilt.","target":"t-1b87"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
